Population: Active monthly subscribers at the start of a three-month term
Eligibility: Active subscription at the first monthly renewal price; A renewal price set by the pricing engine in each of months 1 to 3; One account per customer, so shared-household accounts are excluded; A three-month term that starts at time zero, with no exit before the month-3 renewal
Follow-up starts: The first monthly renewal price, after the usage score and the month-1 engagement score and before the engine sets the price
Strategies: The pricing engine's own price in months 1 to 3; Raise each monthly price by a declared factor where the raised price stays inside that month's price band, otherwise keep the engine's price. The question uses a 12% rise, and the support step also reads 6% and 25%; Cut each monthly price by 15% where the cut price stays inside that month's price band, otherwise keep the engine's price
Versions: The renewal price the engine quotes, not rounded; The declared factor on the engine's price, quoted for one month; The 15% cut on the engine's price, quoted for one month
Outcome: Renewal at the month-3 price, and month-3 revenue: the renewal times the month-3 price
Horizon: Month 3, at the renewal after the third monthly price
Intercurrent events: None: the three-month term has no exit before the month-3 renewal; Every customer in the data has all three prices and the renewal, so the data have no censoring
Interference unit: Individual customer
Rationale: The pricing engine logs every input it reads, so usage and the monthly engagement score cover the common causes of the price, the later engagement, and the renewal. This is sequential randomization given the recorded history; A price band that moves with engagement is declared for each month, so the policy keeps every price inside the support of the engine's price; A declared factor on the quoted price, for one month, makes each price one well-defined action, so a customer's recorded outcome is the outcome they would have had under the prices they got; One account per customer and no reference-price spillover support no interference
