Notes:
[1] Shuffled treatment: cleverly replaces the treatment with a shuffled or
    independently drawn copy, so the treatment has no effect and the estimate
    should be about 0. This reads whether the estimator returns the null when
    treatment is independent of covariates and outcome. It does not test the
    effect, and it says nothing about confounding in your data. Each
    trajectory is drawn from a first-order Markov kernel of the observed
    treatments and masked by the observed at-risk pattern. The placebo dose
    keeps each unit's declared band. It moves each dose's position within its
    band, so the placebo dose depends on the covariates through the band. A
    rejection can also show a treatment model that cannot follow the band. At
    each banded node the kernel draws the position from one of the 5 donors
    whose previous value is nearest. For this kind of fit the test gives a
    description only, with no pass or fail.
